{
  "dom_id": "question-133794",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162885/assets/7ad6be914ed14fb22276982edeab75c9726c56e57e32760371db7936b8091468.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Paul's neighbor to the south, Karol, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+2x-8$ square yards, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Karol's plot of land is $x+4$ yards, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Karol's plot width is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nyards.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+2x-8.$\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-8).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-8) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 8 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-4) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-8) & =-7 & \\times  \\\\ -1+8 & =7 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-4) & =-2 & \\times  \\\\ -2+4 & =2 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $2x=4x-2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-8 & ={x}^{2}+4x-2x-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x-2x-8 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+(-2x-8) & = \\\\ x(x+4)-2(x+4) & = \\\\ (x-2)(x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x-2$ yards. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162885/assets/b7bff7b60f02cab37aef8f40d7b303627aedcc37995afc4ffbc2fe756110673a.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
